    "body": "Great on any Friday: Google Pixel Buds Pro 2 (2025) - Bluetooth Earbuds with Active Noise Cancellation\nLow-Mileage Ferrari 488 Pista Demands Access To Your Bank Account\n12 photos\nPhoto: Instagram | motorcarsofchicago\nCan you believe it’s only been six years since Ferrari pulled the plug on the 488? We (or I in this case) though that it is a lot older, but let’s not forget that assembly commenced back in 2015.\nOver the years, the Prancing Horse offered it as a two-door berlinetta (coupe) and with a retractable hard top (Spider), and there have been some special editions, as well, including the 488 Pista Piloti, and the J50. The KC23, P80/C, and SP38 Deborah were one-offs, and the 488 GTB and 488 Spider were joined by the 488 Pista and 488 Pista Spider.\nThese remain sought-after models, and it’s easy to understand why. After all, they are more track-focused supercars than their mainstream models, and it’s worth noting that the Pista’s design was influenced by the 488 Challenger and the 488 GTE racers. Besides the exterior mods, it also had some changes on the inside, mostly with a weight-saving focus, and also boasted more power.\nFerrari fans know that the 488 Pista was 200 pounds (91 kg) lighter than the 488 GTB, and had 49 hp (50 ps/37 kW) and 74 lb-ft (100 Nm) of torque more. The uprated twin-turbocharged 3.9-liter V8 engine was rated at 710 hp (720 ps/530 kW) and 568 pound-feet (770 Nm) of torque, enabling 0-62 mph (0-100 kph) in 2.85 seconds, or almost two-tenths of a second faster than the GTB. From 0-124 mph (0-200 kph), it needed 7.6 seconds, and it hit over 211 mph (340 kph) flat out.\nPhoto: Instagram | motorcarsofchicago Pictured in the gallery is a 2020 model year Ferrari 488 Pista , presented in blue, with orange racing stripes running across its length. It sports anthracite wheels with a V-spoke design, has red brake calipers, an orange leather interior with plenty of black details, a flat-bottom steering wheel with red stitching, black pillars, an orange headliner, and the usual gear expected from such a thing.\nThis is definitely an interesting spec, and while some might argue that it would look best if it were dressed in other colors, others would say that it is simply perfect. Where do you stand on that? Actually, before inviting you to leave your impression on this Ferrari 488 Pista, we also have to tell you that it has in the region of 3,000 miles (~4,800 km) on the clock. Therefore, it hasn’t seen that much action over the years.\nThe selling dealer, which is known as @motorcarsofchicago on Instagram, offers financing, accepts trade-ins, and is asking for a lot of money for this Ferrari 488 Pista . In fact, at the time of writing, the older Italian supercar was advertised for $1,399,995. Keep in mind that this model tends to fetch between $750,000 and over $1.4 million, depending on the mileage, spec, condition, and other factors. View this post on Instagram A post shared by Motor Cars of Chicago (@motorcarsofchicago)\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nferrari 488 pista Ferrari 488 pista for sale used cars USA supercar v8\nAbout the author: Cristian Gnaticov\nAfter a series of unfortunate events put an end to Cristian's dream of entering a custom built & tuned old-school Dacia into a rally competition, he moved on to drive press cars and write for a living. He's worked for several automotive online journals and now he's back at autoevolution after his first tour in the mid-2000s. Full profile\nUP NEXT The Only Numbers-Matching 1970 Plymouth Sport Fury GT 440 Six-Barrel Took 27 Years To Restore",
